	"description": [
		"Students read and discuss children's literature from Britain and the United States. Beginning with fairy tales and classics from the \"golden age\" of children's literature, students explore an array of picture books, poetry, and fiction, that exemplifies the best in fantasy and realism for children and young adults. Offered annually. Also counts toward women's and gender studies major and educational studies and women's and gender studies concentrations. Prerequisite: FYW."
